PART 6 - DEADLOCK: A locks 9201 then 9202, B locks 9202 then 9201
==========================================================================
[Terminal A] BEGIN
[Terminal A]   -> BEGIN
[Terminal A] SELECT copy_id, status FROM copy WHERE copy_id=9201 FOR UPDATE
[Terminal A]   -> ['copy_id', 'status']: [(9201, 'available')]
[Terminal B] BEGIN
[Terminal B]   -> BEGIN
[Terminal B] SELECT copy_id, status FROM copy WHERE copy_id=9202 FOR UPDATE
[Terminal B]   -> ['copy_id', 'status']: [(9202, 'available')]
[Terminal A] SELECT copy_id, status FROM copy WHERE copy_id=9202 FOR UPDATE
[Terminal A] (still running after 1.5 s: True)
[observer] SELECT application_name, state, wait_event_type, wait_event FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE application_name = %s
[observer]   -> ['application_name', 'state', 'wait_event_type', 'wait_event']: [('Terminal A', 'active', 'Lock', 'transactionid')]
[observer] => Terminal A is BLOCKED, waiting for a lock held by the other session
[Terminal B] SELECT copy_id, status FROM copy WHERE copy_id=9201 FOR UPDATE
[Terminal B] ERROR:  deadlock detected
DETAIL:  Process 29109 waits for ShareLock on transaction 65568; blocked by process 29108.
Process 29108 waits for ShareLock on transaction 65569; blocked by process 29109.
HINT:  See server log for query details.
CONTEXT:  while locking tuple (62,93) in relation "copy"
[Terminal A]   -> ['copy_id', 'status']: [(9202, 'available')]
[Terminal A] SURVIVOR: its blocked SELECT returned [(9202, 'available')]
[Terminal A] COMMIT
[Terminal A]   -> COMMIT
[Terminal B] VICTIM: SQLSTATE 40P01 (40P01 = deadlock_detected)
[Terminal B] ROLLBACK
[Terminal B]   -> ROLLBACK
RESULT PART 6: PostgreSQL detected the cycle (deadlock_timeout = 1 s) and aborted one
transaction. Prevention: always lock copies in a fixed order (lowest copy_id first).

